WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.252
Formatting changes how a number is displayed, not the numeric value itself.

00:00:05.252 --> 00:00:13.472
For revenue, comma dot two f adds thousands separators and keeps two digits after the decimal point.

00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:17.577
That makes large monetary values much easier to read.

00:00:17.577 --> 00:00:26.438
For growth, percent formatting turns zero point one five six seven eight into fifteen point six eight percent.

00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:29.528
Different outputs call for different formats.

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:32.518
Money usually needs commas and decimals.

00:00:32.518 --> 00:00:35.578
Rates often make more sense as percentages.

00:00:35.578 --> 00:00:40.808
Scientific notation is useful for very large or very small numbers.

00:00:40.808 --> 00:00:44.609
Good formatting helps the reader interpret the result quickly.
